Package: Triage
Type: Package
Title: Adjudication of Cell-Type Annotations Using Biological Evidence and Cell Ontology Constraints
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Triage", family = "contributors", role = "aut",
        comment = "See git history for individual contributors"),
    person(given = "shaolab-UM", email = "linfanxiao.bio@gmail.com",
        role = "cre", comment = "Repository contact"))
Maintainer: shaolab-UM <linfanxiao.bio@gmail.com>
Description: Triage is a downstream adjudication workflow: it begins after
    candidate cell-type annotations have been generated and adjudicates
    single-cluster annotations from multiple reviewers (CASSIA, an in-house
    marker-based annotator and enrichment-based annotation) using biological
    evidence and Cell Ontology constraints. The package provides the CL-Linker
    deterministic lexical Cell Ontology label mapper, and the deterministic
    adjudication core (normalization, release policy, consensus rules and the
    local validation gate), which runs fully offline. The Handling Editor stage
    can optionally be called through a DeepSeek-compatible LLM API from the
    package; Chief QC and final release-state assignment run only in the batch
    pipeline scripts, not in the package API.
